## Order

1. Lint first: `validate_proposal_spec` has no error (and its checks on `codebase-notes.md` and `change-impact.md`).
2. The fixed checklist of `gate-review` spec mode.
3. The questions below.

Each finding gets a severity (CRITICAL / HIGH / MEDIUM / LOW) and becomes a `Q-NN`. Gate 1 is presented with 0 `OPEN` `Q-NN`.

## How a question is written

Ask about the spec text, not about the product: "Does BR-03 say which role may cancel?", not "Can a manager cancel?". Tag each question and cite what it checks:

| Tag | Means |
|---|---|
| `[Gap]` | Something the item needs is not written |
| `[Ambiguity]` | Written, but readable two ways (vague word, synonym, unmeasurable signal) |
| `[Conflict]` | Two statements, or a statement and a `D-NN`, disagree |

## Every job type

These add to the fixed spec-mode checks (vague words, terminology drift, conflicts, coverage); write only what this workspace needs beyond them.

- Does every BR and AC serve a confirmed `G-NN`? `[Gap]`
- Does any goal, BR or AC use a word other than its glossary term? `[Ambiguity]`
- Does any statement use a word from "Words we never write" ([04]({{ref_04}}))? `[Ambiguity]`
- Can each success signal be observed and measured as written? `[Ambiguity]`
- Is every mandatory edge-case category ([03]({{ref_03}})) covered or marked not applicable with a reason? `[Gap]`

